    "one_sector_note": "ONE RECORD IS ONE SECTOR. There is no repeatable leg group and no add-another-leg affordance, which is what makes the sector counter unambiguous and lets the finalise hook write exactly one line_sectors row with a conflict-update instead of reconciling a list. A multi-sector duty day is two records.",
    "no_attempts_note": "Repeat attempts do not exist on the line. The repeat logic is SKIPPED, not zeroed: a zero would be counted as an observed absence of repeats, which is a different statement from the concept not applying."
